language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ SONET: place nodes on rings so that every pair of nodes with demand shares a ring, each ring holds at most its node capacity, minimising the total number of add-drop multiplexers (node-ring placements).
given n : int
given r : int
$ capacity of each ring: the maximum number of nodes it can host, one entry per ring
given capacity_nodes : matrix indexed by [int(1..r)] of int
$ traffic demand between nodes, demand[i,j] > 0 when nodes i and j must communicate
given demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int
$ config[k,i] is true when node i is installed on ring k (rings and nodes are 1-based in the model, 0-based in the output)
find ring_config : matrix indexed by [int(1..r), int(1..n)] of bool
$ total_adms is the number of nodes installed on rings (one add-drop multiplexer per node per ring)
find total_adms : int(0..n*r)
minimising total_adms
such that
$ the total number of add-drop multiplexers is the number of node placements over all rings
total_adms = (sum k : int(1..r) . sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(ring_config[k,i])),
$ each ring hosts no more nodes than its capacity
forAll k : int(1..r) . ((sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(ring_config[k,i])) <= capacity_nodes[k]),
$ two nodes with a traffic demand between them must be on at least one common ring
forAll i : int(1..n) . forAll j : int(1..n) . ((i != j /\ demand[i,j] > 0) -> ((sum k : int(1..r) . toInt(ring_config[k,i]) * toInt(ring_config[k,j])) >= 1))
